.\" Predator Sense Linux
.TH PSENSED 8 "2026-10-18" "predator-sense 5.0.1463" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
psensed \- Predator Sense Linux root service (fan/profile/lighting/battery control)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B psensed
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Root daemon implementing the JSON API of Predator Sense Linux on the
unix socket
.I /run/psense.sock
(root:wheel 0660): sensor inventory, thermal profile and fan control (hwmon
and Acer WMI fan tables), keyboard RGB, battery charge mode over the vendor
BatteryControl WMI surface, system info built from /sys + SMBIOS + DMI, and
health checks.  The daemon serializes all WMI evaluations on one worker
thread with a minimum inter\-eval spacing (and a larger family switch gap)
because the ACPI SMM handler defers near-simultaneous vendor method calls to
its next periodic window, which turns back\-to\-back calls into 5\-22 s stalls.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
List daemon options.
.SH SERVICE
.B systemctl start psensed.service
(unit installed as
.IR /usr/lib/systemd/system/psensed.service ).
The daemon is stateless; per-user state lives in
.IR ~/.config/predator-sense-linux-*.json .
.SH SECURITY
Listens on a root-owned unix socket only; the WMI path is also gated in the
kernel module /dev/psense\-wmi by a GUID/method allow-mask so arbitrary
vendor method calls cannot be made by clients.  All writes go through the
daemon (the CLI and GUI are unprivileged clients).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/psense.sock
JSON API
.TP
.I /dev/psense-wmi
kernel module ioctl surface used for vendor WMI evals
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR psense (1),
.BR predator-sense (1)
.PP
The vendor WMI surfaces themselves are documented in spec/protocol.md of the
predator-sense-linux source tree; the acer\-wmi platform driver provides the
platform-profile interface.
